cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this software or its results, please cite the paper below.
title: "Grid-Accelerated Pivot REMC for HP Protein Folding on the 2D Square Lattice"
authors:
  - family-names: Rathod
    given-names: Daksh
    affiliation: Dhirubhai Ambani University, Gandhinagar, Gujarat, India
    email: daksh.hiteshkumar.rathod@gmail.com
  - family-names: Desai
    given-names: Khamir
    affiliation: Sarvajanik College of Engineering & Technology, Surat, Gujarat, India
    email: khamir.desai.s@gmail.com
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/OWNER/REPO"
abstract: >-
  A replica-exchange Monte Carlo solver for the 2D HP protein folding problem,
  combining six move operators with grid-based pivot collision detection. A
  controlled ablation shows pivot rotations account for about 80% of the
  improvement over local-move-only search, and a controlled comparison against
  16,384 concurrent independent GPU annealing chains shows that raw parallelism
  does not substitute for replica exchange. On the CAISc 2026 benchmark suite
  (S5-S10, lengths 48-100) the solver matches the best-known 23 contacts on S5
  and reaches 212 of 225 best-known contacts (94.2%) in a single 10-hour run.
keywords:
  - protein folding
  - HP model
  - lattice protein
  - replica exchange Monte Carlo
  - simulated annealing
  - combinatorial optimization
